.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt SYSTEMSETUP 8
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm systemsetup
.Nd configure the machine's settings
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f
.Fl command Op Ar argument
.Ar ...
.Nm
.Fl help | Fl printCommands
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads and changes settings that are otherwise made in System Preferences.
It needs administrator access: run as root.
Several commands may be given at once; each
.Fl set
command takes one argument.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl getdate , Fl setdate Ar mm:dd:yy
The date, kept the time of day.
.It Fl gettime , Fl settime Ar hh:mm:ss
The time of day, kept the date.
.It Fl gettimezone , Fl settimezone Ar zone , Fl listtimezones
The time zone, set with
.Xr tzlink 8 ;
the list has the zones named by area and city, and a zone outside it such as
.Li UTC
is accepted too.
.It Fl getcomputername , Fl setcomputername Ar name
The computer's name, in the system configuration.
.It Fl getlocalsubnetname , Fl setlocalsubnetname Ar name
The name on the local network
.Pq Ar name Ns .local .
.It Fl getremotelogin , Fl setremotelogin Ar on | off
Whether
.Xr sshd 8 Ns 's
job is loaded in
.Xr launchd 8 .
Turning it off asks first, unless
.Fl f
is given, since it ends remote sessions' way back.
.It Fl getnetworktimeserver , Fl setnetworktimeserver Ar server
The server named in
.Pa /etc/ntp.conf .
.It Fl getusingnetworktime
Off: there is no network time service yet.
.It Fl getsleep , Fl getcomputersleep , Fl getdisplaysleep , Fl getharddisksleep
Never: the machine does not sleep yet.
.El
.Pp
The other commands of
.Fl printCommands
(the sleep timers' and wake settings, restarting after a power failure or a
freeze, the power button, remote Apple events, the startup disk) print
.Dq Not supported on this machine.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /etc/localtime
.It Pa /etc/ntp.conf
.It Pa /System/Library/LaunchDaemons/com.openssh.sshd.plist
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr date 1 ,
.Xr launchctl 1 ,
.Xr scutil 8 ,
.Xr tzlink 8
